# Bitwarden Secrets Manager — required secrets
# Create these in your BWS project. The secret name becomes the environment variable name.
# Set BWS_ACCESS_TOKEN in your shell before running start-jamf.sh or start-intune.sh.

# JAMF Pro (start-jamf.sh)
JAMF_URL              Base URL of your JAMF Pro instance, e.g. https://yourorg.jamfcloud.com
JAMF_CLIENT_ID        OAuth2 client ID — create under JAMF Pro > Settings > API Roles and Clients
JAMF_CLIENT_SECRET    OAuth2 client secret for the above client
JAMF_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN   Bearer token(s) required of MCP clients calling this server (comma-separated to allow rotation). Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.

# Jamf Platform API Gateway tools (jamf_list_filevault_status / jamf_list_compliance_baselines /
# jamf_list_compliance_benchmarks / jamf_get_compliance_benchmark / jamf_get_compliance_benchmark_devices /
# jamf_list_blueprints / jamf_get_blueprint / jamf_list_blueprint_components) — these hit Jamf's
# shared platform-api Gateway, a different host AND a different OAuth2 client-credentials
# credential from JAMF_CLIENT_ID/SECRET above. Confirmed live 2026-07-29 against a real
# account.jamf.com Integration credential — this credential has privileges (bulk FileVault read)
# that JAMF_CLIENT_ID/SECRET's own JAMF Pro API Role lacks, but does NOT have Classic API access.
# Optional: unset means these tools return a clear config error rather than failing every other
# JAMF tool.
JAMF_PLATFORM_CLIENT_ID      OAuth2 client-credentials ID from an account.jamf.com Integration (Integrations left nav → create one, choosing the permissions these tools need: read:env:filevault, read:pro:compliance-benchmarks, read:pro:blueprints/read:school:blueprints).
JAMF_PLATFORM_CLIENT_SECRET  OAuth2 client secret for the above Integration.
JAMF_PLATFORM_URL            Token endpoint for the above credential, e.g. https://us.apigw.jamf.com/auth/token — NOT the /oauth2/token path Jamf's own OpenAPI spec documents; the real deployed endpoint differs from the spec (confirmed live).
JAMF_PLATFORM_TENANT_ID      Tenant UUID for the Platform API Gateway — NOT the same as JAMF_URL/this Jamf Pro instance. Comes from the same Integration's details panel at account.jamf.com.
JAMF_PLATFORM_REGION         Optional. Platform API Gateway region: "us" (default), "eu", or "apac".

# Microsoft Intune (start-intune.sh)
AZURE_TENANT_ID        Azure AD tenant ID (Graph app-only client credentials for device data — unrelated to the Entra auth secrets below)
AZURE_CLIENT_ID        App registration client ID (needs DeviceManagementManagedDevices.Read.All)
AZURE_CLIENT_SECRET    App registration client secret
INTUNE_MCP_AUTH_TOKEN  Bearer token(s) required of MCP clients calling this server (comma-separated to allow rotation). Generate with e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`.

# Entra ID auth for MCP clients (both jamf-server.ts and intune-server.ts; not secrets, but tracked
# here alongside the rest so both servers' required config lives in one place)
ENTRA_OAUTH_ENABLED        "true" to accept Entra-issued bearer tokens on /mcp in addition to the static token above. Named per-server in code, but if both servers are deployed from one shared env file (as in IAC/ansible-servers' current playbook), they enable/disable together in practice.
ENTRA_TENANT_ID            Entra tenant GUID. Deliberately separate from AZURE_TENANT_ID above even if the value is the same tenant — different app registration, different purpose, don't couple them.
ENTRA_RESOURCE_APP_ID_URI  Application ID URI of the "Desktop Management MCP" resource app registration, e.g. api://colgate.edu/desktop-mgmt-mcp (tenants requiring a verified domain in the URI, like Colgate's, reject a bare api://desktop-mgmt-mcp)
ENTRA_RESOURCE_APP_ID      GUID app ID of the same resource app. Optional, but needed once any MCP client sends the RFC 8707 `resource` parameter (e.g. OpenCode) — Entra then audiences the token to this GUID instead of the URI above, even on the v2 endpoint.
JAMF_MCP_PUBLIC_URL        jamf-server.ts's externally-visible origin, e.g. https://jamf-mcp.colgate.edu (required only when ENTRA_OAUTH_ENABLED=true)
INTUNE_MCP_PUBLIC_URL      intune-server.ts's externally-visible origin, e.g. https://intune-mcp.colgate.edu (required only when ENTRA_OAUTH_ENABLED=true)
